<title>USA: Fed adds reserves via overnight system RP's.</title>
<headline>Fed adds reserves via overnight system RP's.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve Bank of New York added reserves to the banking system via overnight system repurchase agreements, a Fed spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>At the time of the intervention around 1005 EDT/1405 GMT, fed funds were trading at 5-7/8 percent, well-above the Fed's 5-1/4 percent target.</p>
<p>The Fed intervened in the market on Monday a little before its usual 1130 EDT/1530 GMT time. Analysts said, however, the central bank's move was purely technical and had no monetary policy implications.</p>
<p>-- N.A. Treasury Desk 212-859-1660</p>
